From 100073d6a69539daafb593552d7f81b29c072aac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 36/63] tls: uTLS and REALITY clients as Xray and the browsers
 do

REALITY keeps the X25519MLKEM768 key share and announces Xray's client version; the uTLS hellos of
the browsers are built from their specification (Firefox 148, Safari 26.3, chrome, edge, ios and the
rest); the handshake state is released after the handshake; the TLS dialer reads a pending alert
after data as crypto/tls does; REALITY refuses what it cannot use.

Made of these commits of the earlier series (branch archive/r25-1.14-commits):
  b8464e0cf reality: keep X25519MLKEM768 key share, announce client version 26.3.27
  b6985ee63 utls: firefox -> Firefox 148, safari -> Safari 26.3 (as Xray-core)
  7392caf99 utls: keep the randomized fingerprint consistent
  478cbe204 tls: release the uTLS handshake state after the handshake
  7e4affe4e badtls: read a pending alert after data, as crypto/tls does
  555fd2231 tls: give the connections of the TLS dialer the badtls read waiter
  4e6496d2e tls: name the uTLS fingerprints REALITY cannot use
  67f48d60e tls: do not rebuild the Client Hello after the handshake
  de1ead908 tls: make the uTLS hello of chrome, edge, ios, qq, 360 and android from its specification
  d0485065e reality: refuse a short_id longer than it can be
  28769b0d9 tls: REALITY: drop the loop that did not change the ALPN

Pdk-Feature: utls-reality
Pdk-Zone: protocols
Pdk-Layer: 04
